  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 426 AM EDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nPretty uneventful period this week with the biggest impacts\nbeing the cool, brisk mornings with patches of light fog/mist\npossible each morning. The coldest morning is expected overnight\ntonight into Tuesday morning with lows in the low 40s to upper \n30s especially north of US-6. A few patches of light frost \nespecially on metal vehicles or roof tops may be possible in \nthese same areas but at this time dew points look to stay warm \nenough for mainly dew covering of surfaces. Will continue to \nmonitor as stated previously if a bit drier airmass is able to \npush far enough south into the area that lower lows would be \npossible. Still stressing that if you have temperature sensitive\nplants/animals it would be best to protect them out of an \nabundance of caution.\n\nDry conditions continue through the work week and next chances\nof precipitation look to come by late weekend. High \ntemperatures this week will start out below normal and trend \nwarmer through the week to more slightly above normal levels \n(low to mid 70s). Just for reference current normal high \ntemperatures at Fort Wayne is currently at 69 degrees and 67 for\nSouth Bend.",
